# Skip validation unless asked

Finish the requested implementation, then stop. Do not start tests, browser checks, screenshots, lint passes, or other verification on your own.

- Run validation only when the current message explicitly asks for it (for example "test this", "verify in the browser", "run the tests").
- If validation looks useful and they did not ask, ask once and wait. Do not start it while waiting.
- A prior yes does not carry forward. Each new task needs a fresh ask or an explicit request in that message.
- Validation covers unit and end-to-end tests, dev-server checks, browser flows, screenshots, and lint or typecheck runs done only to prove the change works.
- Reading code and making the change stay in scope.

```text
// User: "Add a filter to the device table"
// Do: implement the filter, then ask whether to verify.
// Do not: open the browser, run tests, or take screenshots.

// User: "Add a filter and verify it in the browser"
// Do: implement the filter and verify it in the browser.
```
